 {"id":"PERF-001","status":"in_progress","priority":"P2","type":null,"complexity":1,"title":"P2 — tests/cli.test.ts pays a ~620ms npx tax on every CLI spawn: 38.90s -> 18.89s (2.06x) by calling the tsx binary directly","reasoning":"MEASUREMENT (2026-11-16, speclang-perf tick speclang-perf-2026-11-16-06-03-30). Hot path: tests/cli.test.ts:125 builds the CLI command with \"npx tsx --tsconfig <cfg> src/cli/index.ts\" and tests/cli.test.ts:127 (cliExec) spawns it once per test. Per-file attribution from a structured vitest run (--reporter=json): tests/cli.test.ts = 49,390ms of 110,577ms cumulative across 101 files (44.7%), the single largest consumer; next is tests/daemon/arch004-autonomous-cascade.test.ts at 15,167ms. PER-SPAWN PROFILE (hyperfine, 2 warmup + 5 runs, same cwd): npx tsx on a trivial file 878.1ms +/- 26.6 vs direct tsx binary 168.3ms +/- 8.0 (5.22x); on the real CLI command (list over 464 specs) npx tsx = 1.062s +/- 0.028 vs direct = 439.4ms +/- 8.7 (2.42x). Mechanism confirmed by exec census (strace -f -c -e trace=execve): npx arm forks 30 execve per invocation, direct arm 4 — the ~620ms delta is npx resolution fan-out, not tsx startup. FILE-LEVEL A/B, same command \"TMPDIR=$PWD/.tmp npx vitest run tests/cli.test.ts --reporter=dot\", same pass set (41 passed | 2 skipped): BEFORE 38.90s (tests 38.41s, loadavg 9.20 -> 7.37); AFTER 18.89s (tests 18.39s, loadavg 6.34 -> 6.99) with the patch in worktree /home/kara/speclang-wt-perfcli at HEAD 08b77a59 (node_modules + dist symlinked). The UNPATCHED control was re-run in that SAME worktree and returned 38.90s (38.41s tests), so the 20.01s delta (-51.4%) is the patch, not the worktree. SUITE LEVEL: main tree 39.22s / 1826 passed | 58 skipped vs patched worktree 19.81s at matched loadavg (7-9). CAVEAT: the patched arm resolved tsx through SPECLANG_TSX_BIN because the shared node_modules has no local tsx, which is itself part of the defect — today the spawn depends on whatever tsx npx resolves (on this host PATH ts